hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24281","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abdullah ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, from his uncle: That Ka'b ibn al-Ashraf used to satirize the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Sa'd ibn Mu'adh to send five men to him. So they came to him while he was in the sitting of his people in al-Awali. When he saw them he was frightened of them and said: What has brought you? They said: We have come to you for a need. He said: Let some of you come near to me and tell me his need. So some of them came near to him and said: We have come to sell you some coats of mail of ours. He said: By Allah, if you do, you have been strained since this man alighted among you, or he said: With you. So they promised him to come to him after a lull of the night. He said: So they came to him, and he stood up to them. His wife said to him: These men have not come to you at this hour for anything you like. He said: They have told me their need. When he came near to them, Abu Abs embraced him, and Muhammad ibn Maslamah struck him with the sword, and stabbed him in his side, and they killed him. When the Jews awoke in the morning, they went early to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Our chief was killed by treachery. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reminded them of how he used to satirize him in his poems and how he used to harm him. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called them to write a document between him and them. He said: So that document was with Ali."
"24282","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, who said: Al-Zuhri said: So Ibn Ka'b ibn Malik informed me, from his uncle: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he sent to Ibn Abi al-Huqayq at Khaybar, forbade killing women and children."
"24283","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Ka'b, and he mentioned similar to it."
